body:
The uniform buffer issue comes here: 
<https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/6b76a5a8dc011723033cc8ad2ba3da345daab039/servers/rendering/renderer_scene_cull.cpp#L3479-L3487>

It shall be (in pseudocode): 
```cpp
const RendererSceneRender::CameraData *prev_camera_data = p_camera_data; 
if (p_viewport.is_valid()) { 
 	occluders_tex = RSG::viewport->viewport_get_occluder_debug_texture(p_viewport); 
 	if (NOT FIRST FRAME) {
 	 	prev_camera_data = RSG::viewport->viewport_get_prev_camera_data(p_viewport); 
 	}
} 
```
If it's the first frame of the scene, just letting `prev_camera_data == p_camera_data` will be correct. `RSG::viewport->viewport_get_prev_camera_data(p_viewport)` will return a different camera transform so that shader would assume that the camera is moving on the first frame.
